                <pb facs="0135" n="102" sameAs="frus:frus1964-68v23/pg102"/>

                <head>75. Central Intelligence Agency Information Report<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d75-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-02-15">February 15,
                        1961</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>TDCS–3/465, 477, Field Report [<hi rendition="#italic">text not
                    declassified</hi>]</p>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Congo Security Report on Death of Lumumba</item>
                </list>
                <p>1. Two security officers who went Elisabethville 10–14 Feb for purpose
                    investigating death of Lumumba returned
                    Leopoldville 14 Feb and reported they had seen and identified body of Lumumba and his two companions. Bodies were
                    rather badly mutilated and showed evidence of having been dead some time. They
                    could not determine from superficial examination exactly what was direct cause
                    death but they did not notice gun shot wounds.</p>
                <p>2. Security officers said no one believes legend of victims having been massacred
                    by villagers 12 February.</p>
                <p>3. Field dissem: CINCLANT</p>
                <p>End of message.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
